{
  "name": "longhorn-beetle",
  "_about": "The Rosalia longicorn (Rosalia alpina), 3 cm long: long and parallel-sided, velvety ash-blue with black velvet marks -- a patch on the pronotum's front, and on each wing case a spot by the shoulder, a broad band mid-way and a spot near the tip; a small spine each side of the pronotum; the ANTENNAE half again the body's length, blue with a black tuft of hair at each joint, swept back; long blue legs with black knees. Variant: the great capricorn (Cerambyx cerdo, black-brown, unmarked). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
